Tenable Web App Scanning, which provides configuration and management of web app scans. The company also provides Tenable Attack Surface Management, an external attack surface management solution; Tenable Security Center, an on-premises vulnerability management solution; and Tenable OT Security, a unified security solution for converged OT/IoT environments that provide threat detection, asset tracking, vulnerability management, and configuration control capabilities to protect OT environments, including industrial networks. In addition, it offers Nessus, a vulnerability assessment solution for cybersecurity industry and enterprise platform; and Nessus Expert, which enables users to programmatically detect cloud infrastructure misconfigurations and vulnerabilities in the design and build phase of the software development lifecycle. Tenable Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2002 and is headquartered in Columbia, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen A. Vintz CPA | Co-CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $862,390 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $501K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $128K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $96K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Tenable Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $4.9B market cap on $999M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 79% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $255M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 19% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 125% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.251061599865888},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $7.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (40% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Tenable (TENB) Down 11.7% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Rebound?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036661/tenable-tenb-down-11-7-since-last-earnings-report-can-it-rebound?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3036661","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795793428.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(TENB) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/TENB_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_112326065402_1795478042.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795478042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Top 5 Market Movers on Wednesday, November 18, 2026: TENB, ANGX, RCEL, QLYS Surge While BLLN Declines","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/top-5-market-movers-on-wednesday-november-18-2026-tenb-angx-rcel-qlys-surge-while-blln-declines","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795075140.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tenable Holdings (TENB) is Finally Winning Back Investors. Here\u2019s What You Need to Know","source":"insidermonkey.com","link":"https://www.insidermonkey.com/news/tenable-holdings-tenb-finally-winning-back-investors-heres-what-you-need-to-know-1867291/","date":"2026-11-1